WEBVTT

00:00:27.164 --> 00:00:30.024
He could read music
before he could actually read.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.315
He played in youth orchestras as a kid,

00:00:32.339 --> 00:00:33.958
prestigious ones.

00:00:33.982 --> 00:00:36.737
Eventually he dropped out
of college to go on tour.

00:00:36.761 --> 00:00:39.145
AB: I went on the road
playing classical music.

00:00:39.169 --> 00:00:40.593
I did that for six years.

00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:43.778
I saw all 50 states
from the back of a van.

00:00:44.082 --> 00:00:45.427
AG: Arthur recorded an album

00:00:45.451 --> 00:00:48.335
that played on classical radio stations
across the country.

00:00:48.864 --> 00:00:51.524
But then something started to change.

00:00:51.548 --> 00:00:54.784
AB: I realized, about age 21,

00:00:54.808 --> 00:00:56.782
that things were starting to go south,

00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:58.982
and I couldn't explain it.

00:00:59.006 --> 00:01:00.558
Ordinarily, classical musicians,